    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW28jYkTEHaVRbSbZqCYEwELz)_\n\n**Reported:** since the vulpea scan was deferred, Emacs hangs for 10+ seconds after init while vulpea reindexes and the dashboard agenda entries fill in, with silent gaps in the echo area.\n\n**Likely cause (read from the code, not measured):** `sp-vulpea-scan-once` ran `vulpea-db-sync-full-scan`, which lists, cleans up and checks dir-locals in the foreground of Emacs; the dashboard's reading of the agenda files visited a vault file and so started that scan; and each of the four dashboard boxes re-read every agenda file.\n\n**Changes**\n- `sp-vulpea-base`: removed `sp-vulpea-scan-once` and its `find-file-hook`. `vulpea-db-autosync-mode` starts from a 5s idle timer after start-up (`sp-vulpea-start-autosync`) with `vulpea-db-sync-scan-on-enable` set to `'background`: files are listed in a subprocess and the queue parses only changed files. Opening a note no longer starts a scan.\n- `sp-dashboard`: the entries of a list of agenda files are read once per draw (`sp-dashboard--read-entries`, cached only during `sp-dashboard--insert-boxes`), and the boxes filter/sort a copy. Until `org-agenda-files` is set (`sp-dashboard-agenda-ready`) the boxes show \"loading agenda files...\"; `sp-dashboard-refresh-agendas` redraws the Dashboard when the files are set, if it is the selected buffer.\n- `sp-vulpea-para`: the agenda-files refresh sets the ready flag and prints messages with the count and time. Autosync start and dashboard reads print their time too.\n- Docs (`sp-vulpea.org`, `sp-dashboard.org`) and CHANGELOG updated; `.el` files edited in step with the docs.\n\n**Not tested:** nothing was run; there is no Emacs in the container and vulpea is not installed. Parens checked only. Profiling steps are in `profiling/vulpea-startup-profiling.md` in the project files. If it still hangs, the profiler will show where.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01E2gmAvaJVa1VjSnfyiQ1n2)_",
